# HanVerse Learn — hanverse-learn
# The logged-in learning app: learn, roadmap, lessons, practice, placement,
# explore, profile, dashboard, parents, admin, auth. Marketing site (landing +
# legal) lives in the separate `Hanverse` repo and deploys hanverse.netlify.app.
#
# This repo deploys to learn-hanverse.netlify.app and serves its own copy of
# the Express API (/api/* -> /.netlify/functions/server), pointed at the SAME
# Neon database as the main site.
#
# Scheduled sweeps (retention-sweep, trial-sweep, league-rotate) are no-ops
# here on purpose — they only run on the main site so emails/rotations never
# double-fire.

## Deploy checklist (Netlify site: learn-hanverse)
# 1. New Netlify site from this repo; set site name learn-hanverse
#    (or add custom domain learn-hanverse.<yours>) so the URL is
#    https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app
# 2. Set the environment variables below (same values as the main site,
#    except PUBLIC_SITE_URL / FRONTEND_URL / URL which point HERE):
#      DATABASE_URL  NEON_DATABASE_URL  JWT_SECRET
#      OPENAI_API_KEY  PANDA_CHAT_MODEL
#      STRIPE_SECRET_KEY  STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#      BREVO_SMTP_KEY  BREVO_SMTP_USER  EMAIL_FROM
#      PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app
#      FRONTEND_URL=https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app
#      URL=https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app
#      NODE_ENV=production
#      ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://hanverse.netlify.app,https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app
# 3. Stripe webhook: keep pointing at the MAIN site webhook URL, or repoint
#    it to https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app/api/stripe/webhook (either works;
#    both sites run the same backend code against the same DB).
# 4. Push to GitHub -> Netlify deploy.

DB_USER=your-db-user
DB_HOST=your-neon-host
DB_NAME=your-db-name
DB_PASSWORD=your-db-password
DB_PORT=5432

BREVO_SMTP_KEY=your-brevo-smtp-key
BREVO_SMTP_USER=your-brevo-smtp-user
EMAIL_FROM=HanVerse <no-reply@yourdomain>

FRONTEND_URL=https://learn-hanverse.netlify.app

PORT=3000
HOST=localhost
NODE_ENV=development
